nathanbrgrn@gmail.com wrote:
> Is there a web archive of great NetHack players?
> What are some players to watch?
> Any tips? :)

Go to a server like NAO (http://www.alt.org/nethack/), have a peek into
the running games (telnet to nethack.alt.org), if you found players who
are already in the mazes memorize their names and try to follow those
players in subsequent sessions from the beginning. You may as well
download the ttyrecs from those players if you don't want to wait for a
live session (http://www.alt.org/nethack/browsettyrec.php). You may as
well inspect some of the highscore lists maintained there to get names
of good players; I'd suggest to use players from the "Average deepest
dungeon level reached" list (http://www.alt.org/nethack/avg_dlvl.html).

